        "productionStatus": "production",
        "availability": "restricted",
        "origin": "canon",
        "lore": "Product of the Joint Tactical Surface Fighter Development Program (XFJ Program), begun in 2001 to break through the Type-94 Shiranui's development ceiling using American data and technology. Boening partnered with Fugaku, Mitsuhishi and Kawazaki. The targets were mobility on a par with foreign third-generation TSFs such as the EF-2000 and F-22A, at least 30% more operating time, and less performance lost to equipment weight. Developed in stages at Yukon Base under Project PROMINENCE, it went into Imperial Japanese service as the Type-04 in 2004. The Shiranui Kai is a later rebuild of Type-04 airframes.",
        "attribution": "wiki",
        "publishStatus": "published"
      }
    },
